                        "glosses": [
                            "Of animals, plants, or substances: extremely venomous or poisonous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cf5fa51e-c015-38c9-b16b-14b00360e601",
                        "entry_id": "0be827bc-e266-3855-b8bf-5d305aeb5ab4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Extremely hostile or malicious; intensely acrimonious."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d54b632-4faf-44d1-8852-beb5585e5ffc",
                                "sense_id": "cf5fa51e-c015-38c9-b16b-14b00360e601",
                                "text": "The politicians were virulent in their hatred of the president."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "35f22162-e66e-4f93-a708-714b51ae75b2",
                                "sense_id": "cf5fa51e-c015-38c9-b16b-14b00360e601",
                                "text": "More venemous and much more virulent / Then any poyſoned tode, or any ſerpent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "001f4348-3be4-47bd-85ce-bb5a8e669317",
                                "sense_id": "cf5fa51e-c015-38c9-b16b-14b00360e601",
                                "text": "It was a casual sneer, obviously one of a long line. There was hatred behind it, but of a quiet, chronic type, nothing new or unduly virulent, and he was taken aback by the flicker of amazed incredulity that passed over the younger man's ravaged face."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3e3a897-d161-317a-b8f0-6331de99a878",
                        "entry_id": "0be827bc-e266-3855-b8bf-5d305aeb5ab4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of a disease or disease-causing agent: malignant, able to cause damage to the host."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c402c340-1eb9-3d58-8421-c6d008ea598a",
                        "entry_id": "0be827bc-e266-3855-b8bf-5d305aeb5ab4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of a pathogen: replicating within its host cell, then immediately causing it to undergo lysis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
